 \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On the same edit, the Tax Related switch was toggled from off to on (via update action, not just create) and saved. The transaction's Tax column changed from blank to \\\"✓\\\" after the update, confirming tax-related status can be toggled on update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined Type=Income + Category=Consulting + Date range (Dec1-Dec8 2024) + Search=\\\"INV-002\\\" narrowed results to exactly 1 transaction satisfying all criteria (Consulting Fee - Strategy Session, INV-002). Clicking Clear Filters restored the full 20-row transaction list with original totals (+$47,592.50 / -$36,605.99).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Add Expense\\\" with empty Description and Amount fields did not create a transaction (row count unchanged) and did not close the dialog. Both fields have native HTML5 `required` attribute; browser constraint validation returns \\\"Please fill out this field.\\\" for both, and focus moved to the Description field, identifying the missing required info to the user.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid date range not rejected or explained\", \"actual\": \"Setting From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-12-01 (start after end) does not produce any validation error or explanation. The app silently applies the filter and shows \\\"No transactions found / Try adjusting your filters\\\", giving no indication that the date range itself is invalid.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing validation for required category field\", \"actual\": \"Submitted Add Transaction form with Description=\\\"CS-23 No Category Test\\\", Amount=50, and no Category selected. The app accepted it: a new row \\\"Aug 25, 2026 | CS-23 No Category Test | (blank category cell) | — | -$50.00\\\" was added to the transactions table (Total Expenses increased from $36,605.99 to $36,655.99), and the dialog closed with no error message. The category select element has no `required` attribute, so nothing blocks or identifies a missing category to the user.\", \"evidence\": \"Transaction row ref=e2713 shows description \\\"CS-23 No Category Test\\\" with an empty category cell (ref=e2722, no text) and amount -$50.00.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category deletion not blocked when in use\", \"actual\": \"Clicked delete on the \\\"Rent\\\" category, which had 3 assigned transactions totaling $4,450. The confirmation dialog only showed a generic warning (\\\"Are you sure you want to delete this category? Transactions using this category will not be deleted.\\\") with no reassignment option or blocking mechanism. Confirming the delete succeeded immediately: Expense Categories count dropped from 8 to 7 and \\\"Rent\\\" was removed from the list entirely, with no error or reassignment prompt. The 3 transactions that referenced \\\"Rent\\\" are now orphaned (left with an invalid/missing category reference), same as observed in the CS-23 test where transactions can have blank categories.\", \"evidence\": \"Expense Categories header changed from \\\"(8)\\\" to \\\"(7)\\\" and the \\\"Rent\\\" card (3 transactions, $4,450) is no longer present in the list after confirming deletion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding a current-month (Aug 2026) income transaction of $1,234.56, Dashboard Monthly Income updated from $0 to $1,235, Net Profit/Loss updated to $1,235, and Recent Transactions list now shows the new transaction first.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After toggling the \\\"FT-7 Updated Transaction Test\\\" transaction's Tax Related switch on (previously off/unmarked), it immediately appeared in the Tax Summary's \\\"All Tax-Related Transactions\\\" list (1 transaction) and was included in Total Deductible Expenses ($50.00) and the Rent category breakdown, confirming marking tax-related updates its inclusion in the annual tax summary.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Categories page \\\"Rent\\\" category now shows \\\"3 transactions\\\" and Total \\\"$4,450\\\" (previously 2 transactions / $4,400 for the two $2,200 Dec/Nov rent entries), correctly reflecting the addition of the recategorized $50 transaction. Category counts/totals update live when transactions are created/recategorized.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked \\\"Print Report\\\" button on the Tax Summary page (year 2026 selected). Page remained on /tax-summary with no new console errors (0 errors, 5 warnings before and after the click) and no crash/blank page — the print action completed without an application error.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table displays columns Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, and Tax (✓/blank) for every row, and a footer summary shows \\\"Total Income +$47,592.50\\\" and \\\"Total Expenses -$36,655.99\\\" reflecting the current filtered result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Reports page for August 2026 shows Total Income $0, Total Expenses $170, Net Profit/Loss -$170. This correctly sums the two August 2026 expense transactions: QA Small Expense Test ($120, Office Supplies) + FT-7 Updated Transaction Test ($50, now shown as \\\"Unknown\\\" category after the Rent category was deleted). Expenses by Category breakdown (Office Supplies $120 + Unknown $50 = $170) is internally consistent with the summary cards, confirming monthly totals accurately reflect underlying transaction data.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision for values below $500, indistinguishable from zero\", \"actual\": \"After adding a $120 current-month expense (Monthly Expenses card correctly shows $120), the \\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" trend chart's Y-axis tick labels are all \\\"$0k\\\" (Mar-Jul: $0k, and the visible ticks for Aug also read $0k), identical to how a $0 value would be displayed. The $120 non-zero value cannot be visually distinguished from zero via the axis labels.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
